      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1341",
      "html": "<p>Scientific name: Pogonopoma wertheimeri (Steindachner, 1867).</p><p>Type locality: Rio Mucuri District, Santa Clara, Bahia State, Brazil.</p><p>Maximum size: 223 mm SL.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1341",
      "html": "<p>South America: Mucuri and São Mateus River basins. Currently known from three coastal river drainages in southeastern Brazil: the Mucuri River in Bahia State and the São Mateus River in Espirito Santo State.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1341",
      "html": "<p>Usually found in stretches of river with mid to strong water current and rocky or sandy bottom, although some specimens were collected from a lentic habitat.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1341",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1341",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: (Greek) Pogon = beard + (Greek) op = eye + (Greek) poma = lid, operculum. Pronunciation: pog ON oh poma.</p>"
    },
